      "reasoning": "Student correctly derived a = 0.11 m/s². Confirm and move to tension equation. Remind them of forces on the 3 kg block: weight down, tension up, net = ma. Ask them to write the equation and solve for T.",
      "content": "Well done – that acceleration looks right.\nNow look at the forces on the 3 kg block:\n* Downward weight: \\(mg\\)\n* Upward tension: \\(T\\)\nApplying Newton's 2nd law gives\n$$mg - T = m a.$$ \nPlug in \\(m = 3\\,\\text{kg}\\), \\(g = 9.8\\,\\text{m·s}^{-2}\\) and \\(a = 0.11\\,\\text{m·s}^{-2}\\). What value do you obtain for \\(T\\)?"
